  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "e2e_nlg",
  "description": "The E2E dataset is used for training end-to-end, data-driven natural language generation systems in the restaurant domain, which is ten times bigger than existing, frequently used datasets in this area.\nThe E2E dataset poses new challenges:\n(1) its human reference texts show more lexical richness and syntactic variation, including discourse phenomena;\n(2) generating from this set requires content selection. As such, learning from this dataset promises more natural, varied and less template-like system utterances.\n\nE2E is released in the following paper where you can find more details and baseline results:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1706.09254",
  "alternateName": [
    "tuetschek/e2e_nlg",
    "End-to-End NLG Challenge"
  ],
  "creator": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Ondrej Dusek",
    "url": "https://huggingface.co/tuetschek"
  },
